# Netlify redirects.
#
# The live site currently answers on two URLs for every page — /services and
# /services.html both return 200 — because the deployed files are flat
# (services.html at the root) and Netlify also serves them extensionless.
#
# This repo uses services/index.html instead, so the .html forms stop existing
# on the next deploy. These rules make them 301 to the real URL rather than
# 404, which keeps any link or bookmark pointing at the .html version working
# and folds its ranking signals onto the URL we actually use.

/index.html       /            301
/services.html    /services    301
/about.html       /about       301
/contact.html     /contact     301
